AccountV3EntryPoint with official EntryPoint v0.9 source
├── undeployed counterfactual account
│   ├── valid possession and UserOp signature -> create, validate, execute, charge prefund
│   ├── bad possession -> rollback creation and prefund
│   ├── bad UserOp signature or tampered gas -> rollback creation and prefund
│   ├── creation or operation window excluded -> rollback at EntryPoint validation
│   ├── two ECDSA signers and counterfactual prefund -> fit 500,000 verification gas
│   ├── canonical estimation slack -> also fit 496,000 without changing prefund/signatures
│   └── valid validation but reverted execution -> preserve account, charge gas, consume nonce
├── already deployed account
│   ├── stale initCode -> ignore without resetting authority or creation window
│   ├── replay -> reject nonce
│   └── two signed operations -> validate and execute both
├── pending creation (isolated SenderCreator caller fixture)
│   ├── external security transitions -> blocked until EntryPoint validation
│   └── expired validation -> reject and preserve persistent pending window
├── direct caller is not EntryPoint -> reject validation and execution
└── validation trace
    └── factory/account/linked-initializer frames must not read clock, balances or EntryPoint code

These tests use full production Account V3 validation/execution and both linked libraries.
The acknowledgement is an external action invoked through the real signed CALL path.
They do not claim bundler admission, remote deployment, physical passkeys or a mainnet gate.
